    "updated_at": "2016-06-01T23:26:41Z",
    "body": "It might.  Another workaround is to not pass around vectors by value.  Use `[]float32` or `*[4]float32` everywhere.  (It is a bit odd that your `add` takes `*vec4` as args but returns a `vec4`.  It might be better anyway to do `func (r *vec4) add(v0, v1 *vec4)`)\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
