    "updated_at": "2016-10-17T17:46:25Z",
    "body": "I believe it does not decompose arrays because it doesn't know how to handle non-constant indexing. There is a TODO in gc/ssa.go:\n\n```\n    case TARRAY:\n        // We can't do arrays because dynamic indexing is\n        // not supported on SSA variables.\n        // TODO: maybe allow if length is <=1?  All indexes\n        // are constant?  Might be good for the arrays\n        // introduced by the compiler for variadic functions.\n```\n",
