    "created_at": "2016-10-21T03:13:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-21T03:13:58Z",
    "body": "Interesting. So the old back end, because it just worked on stack words, saw that these words were being used, never had their address taken, and completely registerized them. And SSA isn't smart enough to do that because it decides about variable tracking early? The implication here, though, is that all the array refs are constant indexes. Maybe if you know the array is only ever accessed by constant index (and address not taken, but that's needed for structs already) then it can be split apart?\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
